{
  "dom_id": "step-q117988",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14268062/assets/58bfea581646e957b4353c8e6383b84bc54997f2b1ffb7d59581a93c2df8d7d4.png)\n\nDetermine the lateral surface area of the cylinder above.",
  "worked_solution": "We can calculate the lateral surface area of a cylinder using the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{L}=2\\pi rh,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius and $h$ is the height of the cylinder.\n\nSubstituting $r=5\\,\\text{mm}$ and $h=2\\,\\text{mm}$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{L} & =2\\pi (5)(2)=20\\pi \\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
